      {
        "pageid": 193458922,
        "ns": 6,
        "title": "File:Wikimedian of the Year 2025 — Wikimania Village Pump — Wikimania 2025 in Nairobi, Kenya.webm",
        "imagerepository": "local",
        "imageinfo": [
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-06-06T14:36:02Z",
            "user": "Exec8",
            "size": 1066564315,
            "width": 1920,
            "height": 1080,
            "duration": 3583.42,
            "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/Wikimedian_of_the_Year_2025_%E2%80%94_Wikimania_Village_Pump_%E2%80%94_Wikimania_2025_in_Nairobi%2C_Kenya.webm?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
            "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wikimedian_of_the_Year_2025_%E2%80%94_Wikimania_Village_Pump_%E2%80%94_Wikimania_2025_in_Nairobi,_Kenya.webm",
            "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=193458922",
            "sha1": "f5746fcb385371c121791e10d1cc7250c31a5b46",
            "extmetadata": {
              "ObjectName": {
                "value": "Wikimedian of the Year 2025 — Wikimania Village Pump — Wikimania 2025 in Nairobi, Kenya",
                "source": "mediawiki-metadata"
              },
              "Categories": {
                "value": "Robert Sim at Wikimania 2025|Nitesh Gill at Wikimania 2025|Wikimania 2025 Village Pump podcast",
                "source": "commons-categories",
                "hidden": ""
              },
              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "Wikimedian of the Year 2025 — Wikimania Village Pump — Wikimania 2025 in Nairobi, Kenya\n<p>The 2025 Wikimania village pump session features an interview with Robert Sim of Singapore, who received the Wikimedian of the Year award, and Nitesh Gill of India, who was designated as an honorable mention. The discussion is hosted by Butch Bustria of the Philippines and takes place in Nairobi, Kenya. During the opening segment, the participants describe their reactions to the recognition. Robert Sim views the award as a validation of the time and effort contributed by the community, while Nitesh Gill expresses surprise and appreciation for the support received from her peers.\n</p><p>The conversation shifts to the professional background of the contributors. Robert Sim discusses his editing focus on Singaporean articles, noting that he transitioned into active editing around 2019. He explains that the motivation for his work stems from a need to update content to meet existing standards, such as those regarding the biographies of living persons and corporate notability. He notes that the collaborative effort involves several other Singaporean editors who work to maintain the quality of thousands of local articles.\n</p><p>Nitesh Gill details her entry into the Punjabi Wikimedia community, which occurred during her final year of undergraduate studies. She was introduced to the project through an academic assignment and subsequently sought further guidance from Sandeep Gill to continue her contributions. Over time, she increased her participation by engaging in in-person activities and establishing self-imposed challenges for article production. She eventually transitioned into a leadership role within her community, supporting planning and coordination efforts.\n</p><p>Technical and collaborative projects form a significant portion of the discussion. Robert Sim describes the development of an indexing tool designed to curate Singapore related articles. He explains the challenges of managing category trees and maintaining accurate documentation for non-technical users. Nitesh Gill highlights her work on the Wiki Tongues collaboration in 2021, where she helped adapt an oral culture documentation toolkit for multiple languages including Hindi, Bangla, and Punjabi.\n</p><p>The participants share insights regarding conference organization and community governance. Robert Sim discusses his role in the East, Southeast Asia and the Pacific (ESEAP) regional hub and the preparatory council. He emphasizes the importance of remote collaboration and seeking expertise across borders to manage large-scale events. Nitesh Gill addresses the challenges of maintaining member motivation, suggesting that effective communication and personal example are vital for preventing burnout and supporting newcomers.\n</p><p>In the concluding segment, the guests offer perspectives on the future of the movement. Nitesh Gill advocates for increased energy and clarity in strategic regional conversations, particularly in South Asia. Robert Sim suggests that greater engagement with both communities and institutional authorities will be necessary for future development. The interview concludes with advice for prospective contributors, emphasizing the value of starting with small, incremental tasks and developing interpersonal skills to foster productive collaboration.\n</p>\n<dl><dd>Host: Butch Bustria</dd>\n<dd>Guests: Robert Sim, Nitesh Gill</dd></dl>",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "Credit": {
                "value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tl-piLjJgls\">Wikimania 2025</a>",
